   "daf": "42a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "מֵי תַשְׁמִישׁוֹ שֶׁל נַחְתּוֹם וְכוּ׳. תָּנֵי חֲדָא: שׁוֹפְכִין בִּמְקוֹם מִדְרוֹן, וְאֵין שׁוֹפְכִין בִּמְקוֹם הָאֶישְׁבּוֹרֶן. וְתַנְיָא אִידַּךְ: שׁוֹפְכִין בִּמְקוֹם הָאֶישְׁבּוֹרֶן!",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «Water that has been used by a baker» for cooling his hands or washing dishes must be poured out, as it contains a small, undefined quantity of leavened dough. «It was taught» in «one» baraita: «One» may «pour out» this water «in a place with an incline, and he» may «not pour» it «out in a» level «place where» the water «collects. And it was taught» in «another» baraita: «One» may even «pour out» this water «in a» level «place where» the water «collects.»"
  }
